COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[501,"§Al-Jathiyah\ndeeds\nTry to list your mistakes and sins that you did or uttered during the last week only.\nSay, \"O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my hearing, and light in my sight.\"\nSay, \"O Allah, guide me with those whom You have guided, keep me safe with those whom You have kept safe, and be an ally to me along with those whom You are an ally to.\"\nguid\nKnow that the worst abandonment is when Allah causes you to stray despite your knowledge.\nYour guidance, happiness and success are in Allah’s hands alone, so ask Him for them.\nReckon with yourself before you are reckoned with.\nrefl\nأَفَرَءَيۡتَ مَنِ ٱتَّخَذَ إِلَٰهَهُۥ هَوَىٰهُ وَأَضَلَّهُ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ عِلۡمٖ وَخَتَمَ عَلَىٰ سَمۡعِهِۦ وَقَلۡبِهِۦ وَجَعَلَ عَلَىٰ بَصَرِهِۦ غِشَٰوَةٗ فَمَن يَهۡدِيهِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ٱللَّهِۚ أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٢٣\n(The one who took his whims as his god), he obeyed his whims until it became his god. Ibn Juzay: 2/328.\nHow do whims become a god besides Allah?\nأَفَرَءَيۡتَ مَنِ ٱتَّخَذَ إِلَٰهَهُۥ هَوَىٰهُ وَأَضَلَّهُ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ عِلۡمٖ وَخَتَمَ عَلَىٰ سَمۡعِهِۦ وَقَلۡبِهِۦ وَجَعَلَ عَلَىٰ بَصَرِهِۦ غِشَٰوَةٗ فَمَن يَهۡدِيهِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ٱللَّهِۚ أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٢٣\nThis verse contains a scathing rebuke for following one’s own whims. Ibn Abbas said: Every time Allah mentions the whim, it is censured. Wahb said: When you try to decide the best between two courses of action, do the one that is far from your whims. Sahl Al-Tustari said: Your whim is your sickness, but if you go against it, it becomes your medicine. Al-Alusi: 25/209.\nHow does one deals wisely with his whims and desires for sins?\nأَفَرَءَيۡتَ مَنِ ٱتَّخَذَ إِلَٰهَهُۥ هَوَىٰهُ وَأَضَلَّهُ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ عِلۡمٖ وَخَتَمَ عَلَىٰ سَمۡعِهِۦ وَقَلۡبِهِۦ وَجَعَلَ عَلَىٰ بَصَرِهِۦ غِشَٰوَةٗ فَمَن يَهۡدِيهِ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ٱللَّهِۚ أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٢٣\nThis verse cautions the believers against following their whims when performing their good deeds and abandoning the true proofs. When one likes the truth, then it becomes a trait of him to always follow its proof. Just like when the believer loves the prayers, congregation, nighttime prayers during the month of Ramadan, and the recital of the Quran. In one Hadith, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"O Bilal, give us comfort by it,\" which refers to Iqamah for prayer. As for following a desired matter to satisfy one’s own whims without evaluating whether it is good or evil, then this is a cause for misguidance and evil intention. Ibn Ashur: 25/359.\nThis verse contains a fundamental principle about following one’s own whims. What is it?.\nوَإِذَا تُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتُنَا بَيِّنَٰتٖ مَّا كَانَ حُجَّتَهُمۡ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُواْ ٱئۡتُواْ بِـَٔابَآئِنَآ إِن كُنتُمۡ صَٰدِقِينَ ٢٥\nDue to the high status of the Prophet (ﷺ), Allah honored this Muslim Ummah by not responding to the polytheists' request to bring their forefathers from the dead, as His divine ways entail that whoever does not believe after witnessing a miracle, will surely perish just as was done to former nations. Al-Biqai: 7/106.\nAllah honored this Muslim Ummah by not responding to the polytheists’ request to bring their forefathers from the dead. Explain.\nوَإِذَا تُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتُنَا بَيِّنَٰتٖ مَّا كَانَ حُجَّتَهُمۡ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُواْ ٱئۡتُواْ بِـَٔابَآئِنَآ إِن كُنتُمۡ صَٰدِقِينَ ٢٥\nAl-Zamakhshari said: If you wonder why is their statement called an (argument) while, in fact, it is not? I say: Because they presented it as such, hence, it is called an argument in ridicule; or, because they thought it was an argument. It is as if saying: Their only argument is that which is not an argument. The aim is to show their lack of argument at all. Al-Qurtubi: 19/167.\nAllah calls their saying: An (argument). Why?\nوَتَرَىٰ كُلَّ أُمَّةٖ جَاثِيَةٗۚ\nIn fear and panic, awaiting the judgement of the Most Gracious Sovereign. Al-Saadi: 778.\nWhat is the reason for nations to be on their knees on the Day of Resurrection?\nفَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ فَيُدۡخِلُهُمۡ رَبُّهُمۡ فِي رَحۡمَتِهِۦۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ ٱلۡفَوۡزُ ٱلۡمُبِينُ ٣٠\nEven though the verses begin with mentioning the people of falsehood, (that Day the people of falsehood will lose), the details, however, started by describing the state of the believers to laud them, hasten their joy, and escalate the misery of the people of falsehood. Ibn Ashur: 25/371.\nAllah's honor toward the believers has many manifestations. Describe one in light of this verse.\nwords\nوَخَتَمَSealed up\nغِشَاوَةًA cover\nلاَ رَيبَ فِيهِAbout which there is no doubt\nإِن نَظُنُّ إِلاَّ ظَنًّاWe think it is just an assumption"],[502,"§Al-Jathiyah, Al-Ahqaf\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, help me to remember You, give thanks to You, and to worship You in the best manner.\"\nSay, \"Glory is to Allah and praise is to Him,\" as many as a hundred times in the morning and evening.\nMake a long bow in your prayer today and glorify Allah with all of His exalting attributes.\nguid\nThe false hope to have a long life and delusion by the worldly life are among the causes of punishment.\nRemember that everything you have hidden will be revealed on the Day of Resurrection.\nStay away from mockery and ridicule, especially of religious symbols, as the consequences are dire.\nrefl\nوَغَرَّتۡكُمُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۚ\nThe life of this world had deceived you with its falsehoods and ornaments until you thought there would be no other life or resurrection. Al-Qurtubi: 19/173.\nHow did worldly life delude them?\nفَلِلَّهِ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ رَبِّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَرَبِّ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٣٦\nThe word (Lord) is repeated to allude to the fact that Allah's protection and upbringing of His creations have many aspects depending on their particular affairs; His protection of a certain aspect is different from that of another, and His protection of His creations as a whole is not the same as protecting each one on its own, despite the fact that relative to His Power, all of that is easy. Al-Biqai: 18/116.\nThe word (Lord) is repeated. Why?\nفَلِلَّهِ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ رَبِّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَرَبِّ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٣٦ وَلَهُ ٱلۡكِبۡرِيَآءُ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ\nWorship is based on two pillars: Love of Allah and humility toward Him, both of which stem from knowledge of the praiseworthy attributes, majesty, and supremacy of Allah. A l-Saadi: 779.\nWhat are the pillars of worship? From where do they stem?\nوَلَهُ ٱلۡكِبۡرِيَآءُ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ وَهُوَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ٣٧\nAbu Huraira (t) said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: Allah, the Glorified, says: \"Pride is My cloak and Greatness is My robe, and whoever competes with Me with regard to either of them, I shall throw him into the Fire.\" Al-Shawkani: 5/12.\nFrom the Prophet's Sunnah, show that Pride is restricted to Allah.\nتَنزِيلُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ٢ مَا خَلَقۡنَا ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ وَمَا بَيۡنَهُمَآ إِلَّا بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَأَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗىۚ\nHaving referred to the revelation of His Book that contains commands and prohibitions, Allah now mentions His creation of the heavens and the earth thus combining the creation and the command. (Verily, His is the creation and the command) [7:54]. Al-Saadi: 779.\nAfter mentioning the revelation of His Book, Allah mentions His creation of the heavens and the earth and what is in between. Why?\nوَمَنۡ أَضَلُّ مِمَّن يَدۡعُواْ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مَن لَّا يَسۡتَجِيبُ لَهُۥٓ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ وَهُمۡ عَن دُعَآئِهِمۡ غَٰفِلُونَ ٥\nMeaning: No one is more misguided than those who invoke gods and idols that do not respond to them because they do not hear nor understand; therefor, it is described as (unaware). Ibn Juzay: 2/331.\nInvoking that which does not hear is a form of misguidance and ignorance. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَهُمۡ عَن دُعَآئِهِمۡ غَٰفِلُونَ ٥\nIn describing them as (unaware), Allah likens them to a person who is heedless of what is said to him. These idols are unable to understand anything of what is said to them, just like a heedless person who does not grasp what he is being told. Allah rebukes those polytheists for their bad judgement and repulsive choice of their worship of that which does not reason or understand. Al-Tabari: 22/95.\nAllah describes their idols as (unaware). Why? What is meant by that?\nwords\nوَحَاقَ بِهِمThey will be enveloped\nنَنسَاكُمWe abandon you\nوَمَأوَاكُمُYour abode\nوَغَرَّتكُمُYou were deluded\nوَلاَ هُم يُستَعتَبُونَThey will not be asked to appease Allah\nلَهُم شِركٌA partnership with Allah in the creation of the heavens"],[503,"§Al-Ahqaf\ndeeds\nLook for a religious innovation practiced by people and advise those around you to refrain from it.\nLook for a good deed and precede others in doing it today.\nBegin your day by saying: \"Allah is my Lord.\" then, try to do all acts of worship perfectly on that day.\nguid\nThe Messenger only follows what is revealed to him; this makes it even more so for us.\nSelf-admiration is one of reasons for being far from true guidance.\nSteadfastness in religion has great importance and virtue.\nrefl\nكَفَىٰ بِهِۦ شَهِيدَۢا بَيۡنِي وَبَيۡنَكُمۡۖ وَهُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٨\nAt the end of this verse, there is an exhortation to the Prophet to pardon them for ascribing fabrication to him, which is mentioned at the beginning of the verse. It encourages him to extend kindness to them, and exhorts them to repent to Allah. Al-Biqai: 18/132\nThe verse ends with (the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful). Why?\nكَفَىٰ بِهِۦ شَهِيدَۢا بَيۡنِي وَبَيۡنَكُمۡۖ وَهُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٨\nThis is a threat, a hard intimidation, and a stern warning to them. Then Allah says, (and He is the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful), which is an encouragement for them to repent and turn to Him. It means that despite all of this, if you turn back and repent, Allah will accept your repentance, pardon you, forgive you, and have mercy upon you. Ibn Kathir: 4/157.\nIn His Book, Allah always combines exhortation and intimidation. Explain light of this verse.\nقُلۡ مَا كُنتُ بِدۡعٗا مِّنَ ٱلرُّسُلِ\nMeaning: I have not brought something different from what previous Messengers had. Just as you have heard about them stating that they were sent by Allah, I was too. Hence, why do disbelievers wonder about my Message? This verse can be used to respond to the Christians of present times who defame the Prophethood of Muhammad (ﷺ) using baseless allegations with no purpose except misguiding their masses, as the defamers are intelligent enough to realize their slanders. Ibn Ashur: 26/17.\nUsing this verse, how do you respond to Christians?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَوۡ كَانَ خَيۡرٗا مَّا سَبَقُونَآ إِلَيۡهِۚ\nContrary to this, is the position of Ahl Al-Sunnah who say about any act or saying that has not been reported from the Companions (j) that it is an innovation, for if there was any good in it, they would have preceded us in doing it, because they have not left off any of the good qualities except that they hurried to perform them. Ibn Kathir: 4/159.\nWhat is the difference between the saying of the polytheists and that of Ahl Al-Sunnah?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ قَالُواْ رَبُّنَا ٱللَّهُ ثُمَّ ٱسۡتَقَٰمُواْ فَلَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ١٣\nThey are those who combine the Oneness of Allah, which is the essence of knowledge with the steadfastness in religion, which is the essence of practice. Al-Alusi: 25/240.\nWhat is meant by (those who say, \"Our Lord is Allah\", then remain steadfast)?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ قَالُواْ رَبُّنَا ٱللَّهُ ثُمَّ ٱسۡتَقَٰمُواْ فَلَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ١٣\n(They will have no fear): This indicates that Allah's reverence does not cease when witnessing His Majesty, Subjugation, Omnipotence, Grandeur, and Perfection. When one evokes these great attributes of Allah, he becomes humbled, attains serenity, dignity, and tranquility, which increase his status and wholeness. The negated fear in this verse is that which is worrisome to the soul. Al-Biqai: 18/144.\nWhat is the negated fear in this verse?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡجَنَّةِ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَا جَزَآءَۢ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ١٤\nThe servants' shortcomings persist, hence, they are in need of Allah's pardon and forgiveness, for no one will enter Paradise because of his righteous deeds alone. Everyone has sins for which he needs Allah's forgiveness, (If Allah were to take people to task for what they did, He would not leave a single living being on earth) [35:45]. Moreover, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"The good deeds alone of any person will not entitle him to enter Paradise.\" This does not contradict what Allah says, (As a reward for what they used to do) [32:17] because the servant's righteous deeds are no match for Allah's reward despite the fact that they are the cause for the reward. Therefore, whoever thinks that he has done what is required of him and does not need Allah's forgiveness and pardon, is, indeed, misguided. Ibn Taimyah: 5/549.\nHow do you reconcile the Prophetic Hadith, \"The good deeds of any person will not entitle him to enter Paradise.\" and this verse, (As a reward for what they used to do)?\nwords\nافتَرَاهُHe has fabricated it\nتُفِيضُونَ فِيهِWhat you sayamong yourselves about the Quran\nبِدعًا مِنَ الرُّسُلِThe first Messenger sent to the people\nأَرَأَيتُمTell me\nوَشَهِدَ شَاهِدٌA witness from the Children of Israel, like Abdullah bin Salam (t)\nإِفكٌ قَدِيمٌAn old fabrication\nاستَقَامُواRemain steadfast in faith and obedience"],[504,"§Al-Ahqaf\ndeeds\nAssign time today to please your parents and delight them even with a small gift.\nImagine today that you have carried a 5-kg weight for a full day, then reflect on your mother’s suffering while carrying you.\nSupplicate Allah today while prostrating by saying:\nguid\nWhile bringing you up, your mother had endured the suffering of pregnancy, giving birth, nursing, feeding, cleaning, caring, and guiding you; can you pay her back?\nWhoever is the least undutiful to his parents, it is feared that he will be among those who are threatened by this verse:\nThe life of luxury may lead to arrogance and heedlessness.\nrefl\nوَوَصَّيۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ بِوَٰلِدَيۡهِ إِحۡسَٰنًاۖ حَمَلَتۡهُ أُمُّهُۥ كُرۡهٗا وَوَضَعَتۡهُ كُرۡهٗاۖ وَحَمۡلُهُۥ وَفِصَٰلُهُۥ ثَلَٰثُونَ شَهۡرًاۚ\nThis indicates that the right of the mother is more certain than that of the father, because she bore him with difficulty, gave birth to him with difficulty, and nursed him throughout this time period with difficulty while the father did not share any of that with her. Al-Shawkani: 5/18.\nThis verse affirms the rights of parents but with more emphasis on the mother’s. Explain.\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُۥ وَبَلَغَ أَرۡبَعِينَ سَنَةٗ قَالَ رَبِّ أَوۡزِعۡنِيٓ أَنۡ أَشۡكُرَ نِعۡمَتَكَ ٱلَّتِيٓ أَنۡعَمۡتَ عَلَيَّ وَعَلَىٰ وَٰلِدَيَّ وَأَنۡ أَعۡمَلَ صَٰلِحٗا تَرۡضَىٰهُ وَأَصۡلِحۡ لِي فِي ذُرِّيَّتِيٓۖ إِنِّي تُبۡتُ إِلَيۡكَ وَإِنِّي مِنَ ٱلۡمُسۡلِمِينَ ١٥\nThis verse has guidance for anyone who reaches forty years of age to renew his repentance and turn to Allah with a strong resolution. Ibn Kathir: 4/160.\nThis verse has guidance for anyone who reaches forty years of age. What is it?\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُۥ وَبَلَغَ أَرۡبَعِينَ سَنَةٗ قَالَ رَبِّ أَوۡزِعۡنِيٓ أَنۡ أَشۡكُرَ نِعۡمَتَكَ ٱلَّتِيٓ أَنۡعَمۡتَ عَلَيَّ وَعَلَىٰ وَٰلِدَيَّ وَأَنۡ أَعۡمَلَ صَٰلِحٗا تَرۡضَىٰهُ وَأَصۡلِحۡ لِي فِي ذُرِّيَّتِيٓۖ\nThe time period of maturity is singled out for mention because it is normally the busiest time for a person who makes a living for himself, wife and children. It is also a busy time for a woman with a husband, household, and children. During this time period, both, the man and woman are more likely to be distracted from caring for their parents with kindness, so, they are alerted to keep up their kindness to their parents. Ibn Ashur: 26/32.\nThe time period of maturity is singled out for mention. Why?\nأَنۡ أَشۡكُرَ نِعۡمَتَكَ ٱلَّتِيٓ أَنۡعَمۡتَ عَلَيَّ وَعَلَىٰ وَٰلِدَيَّ\nA blessing to the parents is a blessing to their children and descendants because they will inevitably get some of them and some of their effects, especially the blessing of religious commitment because the righteousness of the parents, that is based on knowledge and deeds, is one of the main reasons for the righteousness of their children. Al-Saadi: 781.\nWhy should one be grateful to Allah for the blessings He bestowed upon his parents?\nوَيَوۡمَ يُعۡرَضُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ عَلَى ٱلنَّارِ أَذۡهَبۡتُمۡ طَيِّبَٰتِكُمۡ فِي حَيَاتِكُمُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱسۡتَمۡتَعۡتُم بِهَا\nThe believer does not exhaust his pleasure during his worldly life but leaves some of them for the Hereafter. However, the disbeliever, who does not believe in the Hereafter, is keen to take all of his pleasures during his worldly life. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/450.\nWhat is the difference in attitude toward worldly life's pleasures between the believer and the disbeliever?\nوَيَوۡمَ يُعۡرَضُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ عَلَى ٱلنَّارِ أَذۡهَبۡتُمۡ طَيِّبَٰتِكُمۡ فِي حَيَاتِكُمُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱسۡتَمۡتَعۡتُم بِهَا\nThis verse pertains to the disbelievers because it says so, (and the Day those who disbelieved are exposed to the Fire), however, it is an admonishment to the pious among the believers. When Omar saw Jabir bin Abdullah buying meat, he said: Do you not fear that this verse may apply to you? Ibn Juzay: 2/335.\nDoes the Muslim become admonished by verses aimed at the disbelievers? How?\nفَٱلۡيَوۡمَ تُجۡزَوۡنَ عَذَابَ ٱلۡهُونِ بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَسۡتَكۡبِرُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّ وَبِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَفۡسُقُونَ ٢٠\nTheir arrogance refers to their disdain for faith and their defiant disobedience refers to their physical sins. Here, the misdeeds of the heart precede that of the physical faculties because physical deeds stem from the intention of the heart. Al-Alusi: 25/250.\nIn this verse, misdeeds of the heart precede that of physical faculties. Explain. Which ones are riskier?\nwords\nوَفِصَالُهُHis weaning period\nأَوزِعنِيImagine today that you have carried a 5-kg weight for a full day,then reflect on your mother’s suffering while carrying you.\nأُفٍّ لَكُمَاFie upon you both, [an expression of distaste and irritation]\nعَذَابَ الهُونِPunishment of extreme humiliation"],[505,"§Al-Ahqaf\ndeeds\nMemorize the supplication for when the wind blows and rain, \"O Allah, I ask you of its goodness, the goodness within it, and the goodness with which it has been sent; and I seek Your refuge from its harm, the harm within it, and the harm with which it has been sent.\"\nDo three good deeds; the first with your hearing, the second with your sight, and the third with your heart.\nWatch images of the ruins of former nations, and record its impacts on you.\nguid\nThe stories of the Prophets console the Prophet (ﷺ) and those who followed him.\nDue to their ignorance and arrogance, the people of 'Ad rejoiced at the clouds that brought their destruction.\nThe scientific, civilizational, and structural developments will not avail anything against Allah's punishment.\nrefl\n۞وَٱذۡكُرۡ أَخَا عَادٍ إِذۡ أَنذَرَ قَوۡمَهُۥ بِٱلۡأَحۡقَافِ وَقَدۡ خَلَتِ ٱلنُّذُرُ مِنۢ بَيۡنِ يَدَيۡهِ وَمِنۡ خَلۡفِهِۦٓ\nThe reality of things, whether good or evil, can become clearer through presenting examples and narration about former people. Therefore, Allah says to His Messenger (ﷺ): (And mention the brother of 'Ad). Al-Alusi: 25/251.\nWhat is the benefit of reminding about the story of people of 'Ad?\nقَالَ إِنَّمَا ٱلۡعِلۡمُ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ وَأُبَلِّغُكُم مَّآ أُرۡسِلۡتُ بِهِۦ وَلَٰكِنِّيٓ أَرَىٰكُمۡ قَوۡمٗا تَجۡهَلُونَ ٢٣\nThe word, (people) is added to the expression (behaving ignorantly) to indicate that ignorance had become a community-wide trait and an essential part of who they were. It is similar to what Lot (u) said to his people: (Is there not among you a man of reason). Ibn Ashur: 26/48.\nIn this verse, what does the word, (people) indicate?\nفَلَمَّا رَأَوۡهُ عَارِضٗا مُّسۡتَقۡبِلَ أَوۡدِيَتِهِمۡ قَالُواْ هَٰذَا عَارِضٞ مُّمۡطِرُنَاۚ بَلۡ هُوَ مَا ٱسۡتَعۡجَلۡتُم بِهِۦۖ رِيحٞ فِيهَا عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٞ ٢٤\nAisha (i) said: Whenever the wind was stormy, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: \"O Allah, I ask you of its goodness, the goodness within it, and the goodness with which it has been sent; and I seek Your refuge from its harm, the harm within it, and the harm with which it has been sent.\" And when there was thunder and lightning in the sky, his color underwent a change, and he went out and in, forwards and backwards; and when the rain came, he felt relieved, so, I asked him (about it) and he said: \"How would I know, it may be as the people of 'Ad said: (This is a cloud bringing us rain). Al-Alusi: 25/256.\nWhat is the recommended supplication when seeing the wind blowing fiercely or clouds?\nوَلَقَدۡ مَكَّنَّٰهُمۡ فِيمَآ إِن مَّكَّنَّٰكُمۡ فِيهِ\nMeaning: We gave 'Ad power and prosperity more than We have given to you (O Quraish), so, do not think that what We have bestowed upon you has never been given to anyone else, or that it will protect you from the punishment of Allah at all. Rather, others were given more power and prosperity than you, but their wealth, sons, and troops did not avail them against Allah in the slightest. Al-Saadi: 783.\nMaterial strength does not avail people anything against Allah's punishment. Explain.\nوَجَعَلۡنَا لَهُمۡ سَمۡعٗا وَأَبۡصَٰرٗا وَأَفۡـِٔدَةٗ\nThe purpose of saying: (And We gave them hearing, sight, and hearts) is to emphasize that they were not short of any physical faculties that may hinder their perception of the truth except stubbornness. This is an allusion to the polytheists of Quraish, which means that you deprived yourselves of the benefit of using your hearing, sight, and hearts just as they did. Ibn Ashur: 26/53.\nWhat is the purpose of saying: (And We gave them hearing, sight, and hearts)?\nوَجَعَلۡنَا لَهُمۡ سَمۡعٗا وَأَبۡصَٰرٗا وَأَفۡـِٔدَةٗ فَمَآ أَغۡنَىٰ عَنۡهُمۡ سَمۡعُهُمۡ وَلَآ أَبۡصَٰرُهُمۡ وَلَآ أَفۡـِٔدَتُهُم مِّن شَيۡءٍ إِذۡ كَانُواْ يَجۡحَدُونَ بِـَٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ\nThis verse and other similar ones indicate that hearing, sights, and hearts do not benefit their owners when they deny the signs of Allah. This affirms that intellect, which is the basis of accountability, cannot, by itself, attain the useful faith and knowledge leading to salvation. Ibn Taimyah: 5/550.\nGuidance is not the fruit of intellect; rather, it is a favor from Allah, the Almighty. Explain.\nفَلَوۡلَا نَصَرَهُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُواْ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ قُرۡبَانًا ءَالِهَةَۖ بَلۡ ضَلُّواْ عَنۡهُمۡۚ\nMeaning: The polytheists claimed that their gods were their intercessors with Allah, and would bring them closer to Him, yet they could not help them nor protect them from His punishment. Al-Shawkani: 5/24.\nThe gods taken besides Allah are helpless in this life and the Hereafter. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nبِالأَحقَافِAl-Ahqaf, the name of their place in the south of the Arabian peninsula\nلِتَأفِكَنَاTo turn us away\nعَارِضًاA cloud approaching\nمَكَّنَّاهُمWe established them and gave them power\nوَحَاقَThey were enveloped\nقُربَانًاDeities by which to approach Allah"],[506,"§Al-Ahqaf\ndeeds\nRecall an act of worship of which you have been enjoined by a preacher or a good advisor, and act upon it.\nRecite the Quran by yourself and loud so that when angels or jinn listen to you, your reward would increase.\nListen to a verse from the Quran, then put it into practice so that you become among the people of the Quran.\nguid\nThe believer concerns himself with teaching and benefiting others.\nThe One Who created the heavens and earth is most certainly capable of bringing the dead back to life.\nPatience is a among the traits of the Prophets and Messenger. It is one of reasons for success in worldly life and the Hereafter.\nrefl\nوَإِذۡ صَرَفۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَ نَفَرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡجِنِّ يَسۡتَمِعُونَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ فَلَمَّا حَضَرُوهُ قَالُوٓاْ أَنصِتُواْۖ فَلَمَّا قُضِيَ وَلَّوۡاْ إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِم مُّنذِرِينَ ٢٩\nMeaning: They politely said: Listen attentively. (They went back to their people as warners), they went back to their people and warned them about what they heard from Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). This is similar to Allah's saying, (that they may obtain understanding in religion and warn their people when they return to them so that they might be cautious [of evil]) [9:122]. This verse is quoted as evidence that the jinn have warners from among themselves but no Messengers. There is no doubt that Allah did not send Messengers from among the jinn. Ibn Kathir: 4/172.\nThe jinn exhibited good manners when listening to the Quran, how? Are there Messengers from among the jinn?\nقَالُواْ يَٰقَوۡمَنَآ إِنَّا سَمِعۡنَا كِتَٰبًا أُنزِلَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مُوسَىٰ مُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡهِ\nThey did not mention Jesus (u) because the Gospel that was revealed to him contained admonitions and exhortations, but very few permissions or prohibitions. Thus, it was, in fact, like a complement to the legislation of the Torah, which is the reference. That is why they said, (revealed after Moses). This was also the way that Waraqah bin Nawfal responded when the Prophet (ﷺ) told him about his first encounter with the angel Gabriel. He said: \"Very good, very good! This is An-Namus (the angel) that used to come to Moses. Ibn Kathir: 4/173.\nThe jinn said (revealed after Moses), and did not say \"revealed after Jesus.\" Why?\nمُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡهِ يَهۡدِيٓ إِلَى ٱلۡحَقِّ وَإِلَىٰ طَرِيقٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٖ ٣٠ يَٰقَوۡمَنَآ أَجِيبُواْ دَاعِيَ ٱللَّهِ وَءَامِنُواْ بِهِۦ\nHaving praised the Quran and highlighted its sublime status, they then called their fellow jinn to believe in it. Al-Saadi: 783.\nThe jinn's way of presenting their speech contains a useful lesson in preaching. Explain.\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ كَمَا صَبَرَ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡعَزۡمِ مِنَ ٱلرُّسُلِ وَلَا تَسۡتَعۡجِل لَّهُمۡۚ كَأَنَّهُمۡ يَوۡمَ يَرَوۡنَ مَا يُوعَدُونَ لَمۡ يَلۡبَثُوٓاْ إِلَّا سَاعَةٗ مِّن نَّهَارِۢ بَلَٰغٞۚ فَهَلۡ يُهۡلَكُ إِلَّا ٱلۡقَوۡمُ ٱلۡفَٰسِقُونَ ٣٥\nThe praised resolve in carrying the responsibility of religion is the determination to pursue purification of oneself and reforming the Ummah. It is based on patience against hardship, its motive is piety and its strength is self-reckoning. Allah says, (But if you observe patience and fear Allah, that is a matter of firm resolve) [3:186]. Ibn Ashur: 26/67.\nWhat are the elements of Firm Resolve?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ كَمَا صَبَرَ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡعَزۡمِ مِنَ ٱلرُّسُلِ وَلَا تَسۡتَعۡجِل لَّهُمۡۚ\n(The Messengers of Firm Resolve) are: Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and Muhammad (p). Based on that, the Messengers like whom Allah’s Messenger was enjoined to exhibit patience are four, and he became the fifth. Al-Shanqiti: 7/241.\nWho are the Messengers of Firm Resolve?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ كَمَا صَبَرَ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡعَزۡمِ مِنَ ٱلرُّسُلِ وَلَا تَسۡتَعۡجِل لَّهُمۡۚ\nHaving enjoined His Messenger with patience, which is the highest virtue, Allah forbids him from haste, which is the vilest trait, in order to maintain the best virtue that leads to victory, so, He said, (and do not seek to hasten [punishment] for them), do not seek hastiness by trying to do something that would afflict them at untimely manner. Al-Biqai: 18/191.\nThe verse shows that a good preacher has two traits. What are they? How?\nكَأَنَّهُمۡ يَوۡمَ يَرَوۡنَ مَا يُوعَدُونَ لَمۡ يَلۡبَثُوٓاْ إِلَّا سَاعَةٗ مِّن نَّهَارِۢ\nThe intensity of the punishment that they will be subjected to will make them forget how long they had actually stayed in worldly life, and the number of years and months they spent therein, as Allah says, (How long did you remain on earth in number of years? ` They will say, \"We stayed for a day or part of a day; ask those who keep count\") [23:112-113]. Al-Tabari: 22/146.\nWhat will make the disbelievers think that they had stayed a very short time in worldly life?\nwords\nصَرَفنَاWe directed to you\nقُضِيَconcluded its recital ﷺ The Prophet\nمُنذِرِينَWarners against Allah's punishment\nوَيُجِركُمHe will protect you\nيَعيَ بِخَلقِهِنَّHe was not wearied by creating them\nبَلاَغٌThis is notification"],[507,"§Muhammad\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to mend your deeds and accept them.\nRead about the Battle of Badr, and reflect on the sacrifices made by the Companions in the cause of Allah and how He supported them.\nStand up for Allah by defending a person, who is not present, from being slandered by another.\nguid\nFaith and righteous deeds result in expiating sins and reforming the hearts.\nStand up for Allah and His Messenger by adhering to the teachings of Islam during times of tribulations and the spread of doubts and lusts.\nStanding up for Islam entails abiding by Sharia commands and refraining from its prohibitions.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ يَشَآءُ ٱللَّهُ لَٱنتَصَرَ مِنۡهُمۡ وَلَٰكِن لِّيَبۡلُوَاْ بَعۡضَكُم بِبَعۡضٖۗ\nFor Allah has power over all things and is able to never let the disbelievers be victorious over the Muslims in any place until the Muslims completely defeat them. (But [He ordered you to fight] to test some of you by means of others) so that Jihad will flourish and it will become clear who is sincere and who is lying; and so that some people will believe sincerely based on understanding and not merely following the group that has the upper hand, for such faith is very weak and can hardly survive trials and tests. Al-Saadi: 785.\nWhen the polytheists defeat the Muslims sometimes, it becomes a trial for the Muslims. What kind of trial is that?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ قُتِلُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَلَن يُضِلَّ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ ٤ سَيَهۡدِيهِمۡ وَيُصۡلِحُ بَالَهُمۡ ٥\n(And set right their state), make the state of their consciousness inclined toward every good, far from every evil, safe from all fears, and firm in faith. When one is killed in the cause of Allah, Allah will care and protect his remaining family in a much better way than he would if was alive. Al-Biqai: 7/153.\nWhat is the meaning of: (And set right their state)?\nوَيُدۡخِلُهُمُ ٱلۡجَنَّةَ عَرَّفَهَا لَهُمۡ ٦\nMeaning: Most interpreters said that when the believers enter Paradise, they will know exactly where their houses are, and will never have to ask anyone about them; it will be as if they had been there since the day they were born. The believer will recognize his rank, wife, and servants in Paradise more than he did in his worldly life. Al-Baghawi: 4/154.\nHow will Allah make Paradise known to its people?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِن تَنصُرُواْ ٱللَّهَ يَنصُرۡكُمۡ وَيُثَبِّتۡ أَقۡدَامَكُمۡ ٧\nThose who commit all kinds of sins, calling themselves Muslims, and saying: Allah will help us [against the enemy], are deluded because they are, obviously, not among the party of Allah whom He promised to help. Standing up for Allah means upholding His religion and His Book, striving to make His Word the highest, implementing the laws of His Sharia, abiding by His commands, and refraining from His prohibitions. Al-Shanqiti: 7/252.\nWhat is the meaning of standing up for Allah? Do those who commit sins deserve to be helped by Allah?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِن تَنصُرُواْ ٱللَّهَ يَنصُرۡكُمۡ وَيُثَبِّتۡ أَقۡدَامَكُمۡ ٧ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فَتَعۡسٗا لَّهُمۡ وَأَضَلَّ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ ٨ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ كَرِهُواْ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ فَأَحۡبَطَ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ ٩\nThis is a warning to the Muslim Ummah that if they abandon standing up for Allah, fighting in His cause, enjoining what is right, and forbidding what is wrong, then Allah will forsake them, cease to help them, and empower their enemy to fight them. Some of that already occurred when defiantly disobedient people took charge because of the negligence of Muslims and falling behind while relying on others. Al-Biqai: 7/155.\nWhat is the punishment for disliking and turning away from the commands of Allah?\n۞أَفَلَمۡ يَسِيرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَيَنظُرُواْ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۖ دَمَّرَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيۡهِمۡۖ\nEvery time Allah mentions \"traveling through the land\" in the Quran, whether physically, on foot or riding, or morally through pondering and reflecting, or both, it indicates taking heed and being warned to avoid the punishment that befell those before them. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/454.\nWhat is the wisdom behind Allah’s command to His servants to travel through the land?\nوَأَنَّ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ لَا مَوۡلَىٰ لَهُمۡ ١١\n(Have no protector) to guide them to the paths of peace or save them from the wrath and punishment of Allah. Rather, their protectors are the false gods (Taghoot) who lead them from light into the depths of darkness. Al-Saadi: 786.\nIf Taghoot are allies of the disbelievers, what does this verse mean: (the disbelievers have no protector)?\nwords\nفَضَربَ الرِّقَابِStrike their necks\nأَثخَنتُمُوهُمYou have thoroughly subdued them\nفَشُدُّوا الوَثَاقَBind the captives securely\nمَنًّاReleasing the captives without ransom"],[508,"§Muhammad\ndeeds\nMention Allah's Name (Bismillah) before eating and thank Him afterward, and do not eat without saying Bismillah like grazing livestock.\nRead a book on the description of the Prophet's ablution and prayer so that you worship Allah with knowledge.\nAsk Allah's forgiveness for your sins, then ask Him to forgive the sins of the believing men and believing women.\nguid\nLook and reflect on Allah's destruction of the cities of wrongdoers.\nBecome ready for the Day of Resurrection with righteous deeds.\nKnowledge is important, for it makes you worship Allah with insight and guidance.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُدۡخِلُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُۖ\nEntering Paradise will wipe out the effects of all the hardships they had faced in worldly life. The bliss of Paradise will be a continuation of the worldly bliss of being closer to Allah but without annoyance or distress, and never desiring to leave because it is their abode. This will be a recompense for being denied the adornments of worldly life in order to free them for serve Allah and enjoy His presence because He loves and honors them. Al-Biqai: 18/214.\nWhat will be the effects of entering Paradise on the Believers?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ يَتَمَتَّعُونَ وَيَأۡكُلُونَ كَمَا تَأۡكُلُ ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمُ وَٱلنَّارُ مَثۡوٗى لَّهُمۡ ١٢\n(And those who disbelieve enjoy themselves) in this worldly life like livestock, have no concerns except to fill their bellies and fulfills their lusts, and are oblivious to what will come tomorrow. It is said that in this worldly life, the believer cumulates [good deeds], the hypocrite adorns himself, and the disbeliever enjoys himself. Al-Qurtubi: 19/257.\nWhat is the disbeliever's biggest concern in this life? What is the difference between the attitudes of the believer, the hypocrite, and the disbeliever toward this life?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ يَتَمَتَّعُونَ وَيَأۡكُلُونَ كَمَا تَأۡكُلُ ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمُ وَٱلنَّارُ مَثۡوٗى لَّهُمۡ ١٢\nThose who deny the Oneness of Allah and reject His Messenger (ﷺ), enjoy the pleasures and perishable adornments of this life just as the livestock which have no concern except for grazing. Al-Tabari: 22/164.\nWhat is the similarity between the disbelievers and the livestock?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ يَتَمَتَّعُونَ وَيَأۡكُلُونَ كَمَا تَأۡكُلُ ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمُ وَٱلنَّارُ مَثۡوٗى لَّهُمۡ ١٢\n(And eat as grazing livestock eat): Happily eating anything to their fill regardless of its source or whether it is lawful or not, for Allah has given them more of this worldly life until they became heedless of Him. Al-Biqai: 18/214.\nWhat is the indication when man is given more of this worldly life but deprived of worshiping Allah?\nفَٱعۡلَمۡ أَنَّهُۥ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ وَٱسۡتَغۡفِرۡ لِذَنۢبِكَ وَلِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِۗ وَٱللَّهُ يَعۡلَمُ مُتَقَلَّبَكُمۡ وَمَثۡوَىٰكُمۡ ١٩\nAbu Musa said: Allah's Messenger said: \"Every morning when I wake up, I ask Allah for forgiveness a hundred times.\" Abdulla bin Omar (k) said: We counted that the Messenger of (ﷺ) would say a hundred times during a setting: \"My Lord, forgive me and pardon me; You are the Pardoning and Forgiving One.\" Al-Alusi: 25/294.\nState an example of how the Prophet (ﷺ) reflects on the Quran and put it into practice.\nفَٱعۡلَمۡ أَنَّهُۥ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ وَٱسۡتَغۡفِرۡ لِذَنۢبِكَ وَلِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِۗ\nSufyan bin Uyaynah was asked about the virtue of knowledge, and he said: Did you not hear what Allah says when He begins with it: (So know that there is no deity except Allah and ask forgiveness for your sin), so He enjoined action after knowledge. Allah says, (Know that the life of this world is no more than play...) until He says, (Race one another towards forgiveness from your Lord) [57:20-22]. Allah says, (Know that your wealth and your children are only a trial) [8:28]. Then He says, (So beware of them) [64:14]. And Allah says, (Know that whatever spoils you obtain) [8:41], then He enjoined action afterward. Al-Qurtubi: 19/267.\nExplain how this verse indicates the virtue of action after knowledge. How?\nوَٱسۡتَغۡفِرۡ لِذَنۢبِكَ وَلِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِۗ\nIf it is the case that the Prophet (ﷺ) is instructed to pray for them, which means asking for their sin to be removed and for them to be protected from the punishment thereof, it is implied that he is to show sincerity toward them, love good for them as he loves it for himself, hate evil for them as he hates it for himself, enjoin them to do what is good for them and forbid them to do what is harmful to them, overlook their shortcomings and faults, be keen that they should be united and in harmony, and that all grudges between them should be removed that could lead to enmity and division that would increase them in sin. Al-Saadi: 787-788.\nWhat are the entailments of asking forgiveness for the believing men and women?\nwords\nمَثوىًAbode\nغَيرِ آسِنٍUnaltered\nآنِفًاJust now\nجَاءَ أَشرَاطُهَاSome of its signs have appeared\nفَأَنَّىWhat good will it do them\nمُتَقَلَّبَكُمYour movements during the daytime\nوَمَثوَاكُمYour places of rest during nighttime"],[509,"§Muhammad\ndeeds\nVisit one of your relatives or call him to uphold ties of kinship.\nRead this page of the Quran, then draw three useful lessons, other than what is already mentioned.\nInvoke Allah to purify your heart, rid it of hypocrisy, show off, and self-admiration.\nguid\nBe among those who are truthful to Allah.\nSevering ties of kinship is a grave matter.\nNo servant ever conceals anything except that Allah is able to expose it.\nrefl\nفَهَلۡ عَسَيۡتُمۡ إِن تَوَلَّيۡتُمۡ أَن تُفۡسِدُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَتُقَطِّعُوٓاْ أَرۡحَامَكُمۡ ٢٢ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَعَنَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ فَأَصَمَّهُمۡ وَأَعۡمَىٰٓ أَبۡصَٰرَهُمۡ ٢٣\nFrom this, it is noted that whoever enjoins what is good and strives against the people of evil, will be safe from corruption in the land and severing ties of kinship. In contrast, if he neglects that duty, he will bear the consequences. Al-Biqai: 7/169.\nWhat are the consequences on society when neglecting the enjoinment of what is good, the forbidding of what is evil, and the Jihad in the cause of Allah?\nفَهَلۡ عَسَيۡتُمۡ إِن تَوَلَّيۡتُمۡ أَن تُفۡسِدُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَتُقَطِّعُوٓاْ أَرۡحَامَكُمۡ ٢٢\nKinship has two aspects: A general and a special. The general is the kinship of religion [the believers]; it must be maintained through love, support, sincerity in giving advice, refraining from harming them, establishing justice and fairness in dealing with them, fulfilling the duties toward them such as visiting the sick, participating in washing the dead, praying for them, burying them, and other required duties. The special kinship is the blood relatives from one’s father and mother's sides. Special rights must be maintained and more such as providing financial support when necessary and keeping in touch with them at times of hardships in addition to the general rights. When maintaining duties becomes overwhelming, attention should focus on the closest kinship. Al-Qurtubi: 19/277.\nWhat is meant by kinship? What are their rights?\nفَهَلۡ عَسَيۡتُمۡ إِن تَوَلَّيۡتُمۡ أَن تُفۡسِدُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَتُقَطِّعُوٓاْ أَرۡحَامَكُمۡ ٢٢ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَعَنَهُمُ ٱللَّهُ فَأَصَمَّهُمۡ وَأَعۡمَىٰٓ أَبۡصَٰرَهُمۡ ٢٣\n(These are the ones whom Allah has cursed), those who spread corruption and sever ties of kinship will be expelled from Allah's mercy. (And has made them deaf), Allah deprived them of benefiting from the admonishments they hear with their ears. (And blinded their sight), He took away their insight so they do not understand Allah's arguments, nor do they remember what they see of His lessons and proofs. Al-Tabari: 22/178.\nWho is being cursed in this verse? What is the consequence of their blinded sight?\nأَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ أَمۡ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبٍ أَقۡفَالُهَآ ٢٤\nIt is as if the heart is a swinging door that is sealed with a lock. Unless the lock is removed, the door cannot be opened and what is behind it remains unreachable. Similarly, Unless the seal of the heart is removed, faith and Quran will never reach it. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/454.\nThe verse indicates the way to opening man's heart for faith to enter. Explain\nأَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ أَمۡ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبٍ أَقۡفَالُهَآ ٢٤\nMeaning: Do they not understand it, and come to know its contents of deterring admonishments, sound arguments, and clear proofs, which suffice those who understand and reason, and deter them from disbelieving in Allah, ascribing partners to Him, and disobeying Him?! Al-Shawkani: 5/38.\nFor one who recites the Holy Quran, what is the sign of his reflection on it?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱرۡتَدُّواْ عَلَىٰٓ أَدۡبَٰرِهِم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلۡهُدَى ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ سَوَّلَ لَهُمۡ وَأَمۡلَىٰ لَهُمۡ ٢٥\nAllah reveals the situation of those who apostatize from right guidance and faith, and turn back to misguidance and disbelief. They do not do that on the basis of evidence or proof that led them to that conclusion, rather, it is misguidance from their enemy, satan, who made that appealing to them and prompted them to do it. Al-Saadi: 789.\nWhat is the reason for some to apostatize from Islam and turn back to disbelief?\nفَكَيۡفَ إِذَا تَوَفَّتۡهُمُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ يَضۡرِبُونَ وُجُوهَهُمۡ وَأَدۡبَٰرَهُمۡ ٢٧ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمُ ٱتَّبَعُواْ مَآ أَسۡخَطَ ٱللَّهَ وَكَرِهُواْ رِضۡوَٰنَهُۥ فَأَحۡبَطَ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ ٢٨\nThe combination of following what incurs Allah's wrath and hating what pleases Him, even though one of them will suffice, alludes to the striking of the angels. Striking their faces befits their following what incurs Allah's wrath, and striking their backs befits their hating of what pleases Him since hatred entails turning one's back. Ibn Ashur: 26/119.\nWhat is the link between combining following what incurs Allah's wrath and hating what pleases Him on one side, and the striking of the angels on the other?\nwords\nمَرَضٌDoubt and hypocrisy\nالمَغشِيِّ عَلَيهِOne who is fainting due to intense fear\nعَزَمَ الأَمرُThe fighting was ordained\nفَهَل عَسَيتُمWould you perhaps\nتَوَلَّيتُمYou turned away\nارتَدُّوا عَلَى أَدبَارِهِمThose who reverted back to disbelief\nسَوَّلَ لَهُمMade their deeds appealing to them\nإِسرَارَهُمWhat they conceal\nأَضغَانَهُمTheir malice"],[510,"§Muhammad\ndeeds\nName three traits of the hypocrites, which are mentioned in the Quran.\nSupplicate Allah to make you among those who are patient.\nSpend some of your allowance today in Allah's way, and do not withhold it.\nguid\nYour belief in the divine will and decree entails patience with trial and calamity.\nBe sincere to Allah in all of your deeds, and do not aim for people approval or praise.\nThe believer feels honored by his faith, hence, he never becomes coward or weak.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ نَشَآءُ لَأَرَيۡنَٰكَهُمۡ فَلَعَرَفۡتَهُم بِسِيمَٰهُمۡۚ\nAllah is telling His Messenger (ﷺ): Had We willed, O Muhammad, We would have shown you the specific individuals who are hypocrites, so that you would plainly know them.\" However, Allah did not do that with all of the hypocrites. He conceals His creation, lets their affairs run according to apparent purity, and leaves the inner secrets to the One Who is well aware of them. Ibn Kathir: 4/183.\nAllah did not reveal the identity of all the hypocrites to the Muslims. Why?\n۞يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ أَطِيعُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُواْ ٱلرَّسُولَ وَلَا تُبۡطِلُوٓاْ أَعۡمَٰلَكُمۡ ٣٣\n(And do not invalidate your deeds), this has four possible meanings, first: Do not invalidate your deeds by reverting to disbelief after your faith. Second: Do not invalidate your righteous deeds by doing bad ones. Third: Do not invalidate your deeds by showing off and self-admiration. Fourth: Do not invalidate your deeds by not completing them. Ibn Juzay: 2/343.\nState the things that can invalidate the deeds in light of this verse.\nفَلَا تَهِنُواْ وَتَدۡعُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱلسَّلۡمِ وَأَنتُمُ ٱلۡأَعۡلَوۡنَ وَٱللَّهُ مَعَكُمۡ\n(And Allah is with you), this contains glad tidings of victory and triumph over the enemies. Ibn Kathir: 4/184.\nWhat will be the outcome for Muslims for being with Allah?\nفَلَا تَهِنُواْ وَتَدۡعُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱلسَّلۡمِ وَأَنتُمُ ٱلۡأَعۡلَوۡنَ\n(Do not weaken), do not be weak concerning the enemies. (And call for peace), do not compromise, call for peace or an end to the fighting between you and the disbelievers while you are in a position of power, both in great numbers and preparations. Thus, Allah says, (So do not weaken and call for peace while you are superior), in the condition of your superiority over your enemy. If, on the other hand, the disbelievers are considered more powerful and numerous than the Muslims, then the Imam (general commander) may decide to hold a treaty if he judges that it entails a benefit for the Muslims. Ibn Kathir: 4/184.\nThe verse indicates the Muslims' position, when they are more powerful, toward their enemy. What should be their position when they are weak?\nإِنَّمَا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا لَعِبٞ وَلَهۡوٞۚ وَإِن تُؤۡمِنُواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ يُؤۡتِكُمۡ أُجُورَكُمۡ وَلَا يَسۡـَٔلۡكُمۡ أَمۡوَٰلَكُمۡ ٣٦\nIt is likely that this verse is a continuation of the one before, (do not weaken and call for peace) as a reminder that abiding by this is the desired piety. Moreover, the love for wealth that can be spent for war efforts may be the reason behind calling for peace. Hence, they are reminded of faith and righteousness so that they may rid themselves of weakness because they are prohibited from showing weakness and calling for peace. Refraining from all that is a sign of righteousness. Ibn Ashur: 26/133.\nGiven this verse, what is the remedy for the weakness of Muslim Ummah?\nوَإِن تُؤۡمِنُواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ يُؤۡتِكُمۡ أُجُورَكُمۡ وَلَا يَسۡـَٔلۡكُمۡ أَمۡوَٰلَكُمۡ ٣٦\n(He does not ask you), He is your Lord. (For your wealth), for giving you your rewards, rather, He orders you to believe and obey so that He rewards you with Paradise, similar to His saying, (I seek no provision from them) [51:57]. Moreover, it is said that this verse means that Allah and His Messenger do not ask you for all of your wealth to be spent for charity, rather, they only ask for a small amount -quarter of tithe- so let your heart delight in it. Al-Qurtubi: 4/163.\nA sign of truthfulness of a preacher is not asking others for money. How can you infer this meaning from this verse?\nهَٰٓأَنتُمۡ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ تُدۡعَوۡنَ لِتُنفِقُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَمِنكُم مَّن يَبۡخَلُۖ وَمَن يَبۡخَلۡ فَإِنَّمَا يَبۡخَلُ عَن نَّفۡسِهِۦۚ وَٱللَّهُ ٱلۡغَنِيُّ وَأَنتُمُ ٱلۡفُقَرَآءُۚ وَإِن تَتَوَلَّوۡاْ يَسۡتَبۡدِلۡ قَوۡمًا غَيۡرَكُمۡ ثُمَّ لَا يَكُونُوٓاْ أَمۡثَٰلَكُم ٣٨\n(But whoever withholds, he in fact withholds against himself), the harm of withholding can only affect him. It is as if he withheld from himself the reward that is due to him for spending. (If you turn away, He will replace you with other people), He will bring others who are not like you, rather, they want to spend in Allah's way. Ibn Juzay: 2/344.\nThe lesson learned from this verse: The requital befits the action. Explain.\nwords\nبِسِيمَاهُمTheir apparent marks\nلَحنِ القَولِThe manner of their speech\nوَلَنَبلُوَنَّكُمWe will certainly test you\nوَشَآقُّواThey opposed and fought\nيَتِرَكُم أَعمَالَكُمDetracts the reward of your deeds\nفَيُحفِكُمInsists and presses you\nأَضغَانَكُمYour resentment"],[511,"§Al-Fath\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to confer blessing upon the Prophet (ﷺ) and grant him peace since that is supporting and revering him.\nPractice on of the Prophet's Sunnah, like Siwak (tooth cleanser), while being aware of the reverence of the Prophet's guidance.\nDedicate time in the morning and evening for glorifying Allah and saying Athkar (remembrance of Allah).\nguid\nThe Treaty of al-Hudaybiya was a great blessing from Allah upon Muslims.\nKeep positive assumption about Allah, for He is as His servant expects of Him.\nFollowing the Prophet's Sunnah, asking Allah to confer blessing upon him, and making his attributes known to others, are part of revering him.\nrefl\nإِنَّا فَتَحۡنَا لَكَ فَتۡحٗا مُّبِينٗا ١\nAz-Zuhri said: There was no greater conquest than that of the Treaty of Al-Hudaybiya, because the polytheists mingled with Muslims, heard their preaching, and accepted Islam. In only three years, many became Muslims, and the number of Muslims soared. Al-Baghawi: 4/166.\nHow did the Treaty of Al-Hudaybiya become a conquest and victory for Muslims?\nإِنَّا فَتَحۡنَا لَكَ فَتۡحٗا مُّبِينٗا ١ لِّيَغۡفِرَ لَكَ ٱللَّهُ مَا تَقَدَّمَ مِن ذَنۢبِكَ وَمَا تَأَخَّرَ\nAllah made this conquest result in many positive consequences. (So that Allah may forgive you your past and future sins), because of what happened as a result of many acts of worship and many people becoming Muslim, and because of what the Prophet (ﷺ) had to put up with of conditions that no one could bear except the Messengers of Firm Resolve. Al-Saadi: 791.\nAllah made the conquest lead to forgiveness of the Prophet's (ﷺ) sins. Why?\nإِنَّا فَتَحۡنَا لَكَ فَتۡحٗا مُّبِينٗا ١ لِّيَغۡفِرَ لَكَ ٱللَّهُ مَا تَقَدَّمَ مِن ذَنۢبِكَ وَمَا تَأَخَّرَ وَيُتِمَّ نِعۡمَتَهُۥ عَلَيۡكَ وَيَهۡدِيَكَ صِرَٰطٗا مُّسۡتَقِيمٗا ٢\nAllah has combined guidance and victory for His Messenger because they form the basis on which success and happiness are attained. Guidance is knowing about Allah and His religion, and working to please and obey Him, hence, that is useful knowledge and righteous deeds. Victory is the full ability to implement His religion through argument and proof, and power and sword, hence, it is victory by words and hands, where those who oppose it are overwhelmed by argument, and defeated physically by force. Allah, the Almighty, often combines these two foundations, as they form the basis by which preaching and prevalence of His religion over all other religions are attained. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/456.\nIn these verses, Allah combines guidance and victory for His Messenger. Why?\nلِّيَغۡفِرَ لَكَ ٱللَّهُ مَا تَقَدَّمَ مِن ذَنۢبِكَ وَمَا تَأَخَّرَ وَيُتِمَّ نِعۡمَتَهُۥ عَلَيۡكَ وَيَهۡدِيَكَ صِرَٰطٗا مُّسۡتَقِيمٗا ٢\nAl-Mughira said that the Prophet stood praying at night to such an extent that his feet became swollen. On being asked why he did this when his past and future sins had been forgiven for him, he replied, \"Should I not be a grateful servant.\" Al-Shawkani: 5/46.\nThe Prophet used to pray to such an extent that his feet became swollen even though his past and future sins had been forgiven for him. Why?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَنزَلَ ٱلسَّكِينَةَ فِي قُلُوبِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ لِيَزۡدَادُوٓاْ إِيمَٰنٗا مَّعَ إِيمَٰنِهِمۡۗ وَلِلَّهِ جُنُودُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمٗا ٤\nAl-Razi said: Tranquility is confidence in Allah's promise, and patience with His decree; in fact, tranquility is a source of victory, strength, and a spirit to which the frightened rests, and the grieving finds consolation. The effects of this tranquility are reverence, humbleness, and firm management of affairs. Al-Biqai: 18/284.\nWhat are the effects of tranquility on the believer?\nلِيَزۡدَادُوٓاْ إِيمَٰنٗا مَّعَ إِيمَٰنِهِمۡۗ\nThe unequivocal truth is that faith increases and decreases, as Ahl Al-Sunnah agreed, and as inferred from the Quran and the Prophet's Sunnah. Al-Shanqiti: 7/394.\nThis verse affirms an important part of the creed of Ahl Al-Sunnah. What is it?\nلِّتُؤۡمِنُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَتُعَزِّرُوهُ وَتُوَقِّرُوهُۚ\nThe meaning of (support) in this verse is empowering through providing assistance and help. This can only be done through obedience, veneration, and respect. Reverence means veneration, respect, and honoring. Al-Tabari: 22/208.\nWhat is meant by: (support and revere) in this verse? How can that be attained?\nwords\nفَتحًا مُبِينًاTreaty of Al-Hudaybiya in the year 6 Hijri\nالسَّكِينَةَTranquility and steadfastness\nظَنَّ السَّوءِAn evil assumption that Allah will not support His religion\nعَلَيهِم دَائِرَةُ السَّوءِUpon them is a misfortune of evil nature\nوَتُعَزِّرُوهُStand up for Allah\nوَتُوَقِّرُوهُRevere Allah"],[512,"§Al-Fath\ndeeds\nMaintain the daily prayer, as it is a covenant that must be fulfilled.\nGive to charity, even a little.\nCooperate with some family members in performing an act of worship.\nguid\nRecall pledges and covenants you had made with Allah or with people, and work on fulfilling them.\nKeep positive assumptions about your Lord, as evil thoughts about Him are a trait of hypocrites.\nCertain faith in Allah's promise is a condition of the testament to the Oneness of Allah.\nrefl\nفَمَن نَّكَثَ فَإِنَّمَا يَنكُثُ عَلَىٰ نَفۡسِهِۦۖ\nIn breaking his pledge, he would be out of those whom Allah promised them with Paradise for keeping their allegiance, so he would harm no one but himself. As for Allah’s Messenger, Allah would help and give him victory over his enemies, regardless of who kept or who broke his allegiance. Al-Tabari: 22/210.\nWho will be harmed when man forsakes his religion?\nيَقُولُونَ بِأَلۡسِنَتِهِم مَّا لَيۡسَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡۚ\nThey did not ask for forgiveness in sincerity, rather, it was done in ridicule, and what is in their hearts contradicts what they say, hence, Allah exposed them by saying, (They say with their tongues what is not in their hearts), which is the way of hypocrites. Al-Shawkani: 5/48.\nWhat was the true intention of hypocrites when they asked Prophet’s (ﷺ) for forgiveness?\nقُلۡ فَمَن يَمۡلِكُ لَكُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ شَيًۡٔا إِنۡ أَرَادَ بِكُمۡ ضَرًّا أَوۡ أَرَادَ بِكُمۡ نَفۡعَۢاۚ بَلۡ كَانَ ٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ خَبِيرَۢا ١١\nNo one can ward off the harm or benefit coming from Allah. Being preoccupied with families and wealth is not an acceptable excuse, because it will not keep you from harm if Allah wills it, nor will confronting the enemy prevent you from attaining good if Allah wills that for you. Al-Alusi: 13/253.\nIs being preoccupied with families and wealth instead of standing up for religion an acceptable excuse?\nبَلۡ ظَنَنتُمۡ أَن لَّن يَنقَلِبَ ٱلرَّسُولُ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ إِلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِيهِمۡ أَبَدٗا وَزُيِّنَ ذَٰلِكَ فِي قُلُوبِكُمۡ وَظَنَنتُمۡ ظَنَّ ٱلسَّوۡءِ وَكُنتُمۡ قَوۡمَۢا بُورٗا ١٢\nTheir evil assumption was made appealing to them because they did not make the positive assumption that the Messenger would return home safely. This mirrored their weak minds and lowly souls that would consider only the first suggestion. Ibn Ashur: 26/164.\nAllah allures the hypocrites by making their evil assumption about the believers appealing to them. Explain in light of this verse.\nيَغۡفِرُ لِمَن يَشَآءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَن يَشَآءُۚ وَكَانَ ٱللَّهُ غَفُورٗا رَّحِيمٗا ١٤\nForgiveness precedes punishment here, (He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills) to reinforce hope in their hearts so they hasten to make up for the past, and it is a prelude for the promise mentioned in this verse, (Say to those who remained behind of the Bedouins) until this verse (Then if you obey, Allah will give you a goodly reward). Ibn Ashur: 26/166.\nForgiveness precedes punishment in this verse. Why?\nسَيَقُولُ ٱلۡمُخَلَّفُونَ إِذَا ٱنطَلَقۡتُمۡ إِلَىٰ مَغَانِمَ لِتَأۡخُذُوهَا ذَرُونَا نَتَّبِعۡكُمۡۖ يُرِيدُونَ أَن يُبَدِّلُواْ كَلَٰمَ ٱللَّهِۚ\nMeaning: They wish to change Allah's promise to the people of Al-Hudaybiya, when He promised to compensate them for the booties of Makkah with that of Khaibar and its conquest and to be exclusively for them. Those who remained wanted that to be shared with them, and that was the change they sought after. Ibn Juzay: 2/349.\nThose who remained and hypocrites were concerned only with booties. Explain in light of this verse.\nفَسَيَقُولُونَ بَلۡ تَحۡسُدُونَنَاۚ بَلۡ كَانُواْ لَا يَفۡقَهُونَ إِلَّا قَلِيلٗا ١٥\n(Rather, you envy us), this is the best that they can come up with concerning this matter. If they were mature enough, they would have realized that their being deprived of a share was because of their sin and that sins have consequences in both worldly and spiritual terms. Hence, Allah says: (Rather they do not understand but a little). Al-Saadi: 793\nWhat is the real reason for depriving the hypocrites of the booties of Khaibar?\nwords\nنَكَثَBreaks his pledge\nالمُخَلَّفُونَThose who remained\nالأَعرَابِThe Bedouins\nلَن يَنقَلِبَWill not return\nظَنَّ السَّوءِ(ﷺ) An evil thought that Allah will not support His Messenger\nبُورًاDoomed people\nأَعتَدنَاWe have prepared"],[513,"§Al-Fath\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\"\nWrite a biography of one of the Prophet's Companions, and share it in a message to emphasize the virtues of the Companions.\nSay, \"O Allah, make my heart righteous.\"\nguid\nWhoever abides by Allah's commands, Allah will ease his livelihood and worldly affairs for him.\nReflect on Allah's kindness and mercy toward His servants.\nThe Companions and those who participated in Al-Ridwan allegiance possessed a great virtue, as Allah was pleased with them and purified their hearts. Hence, whoever reviles them, is a denier of the Quran.\nrefl\nلَّيۡسَ عَلَى ٱلۡأَعۡمَىٰ حَرَجٞ وَلَا عَلَى ٱلۡأَعۡرَجِ حَرَجٞ وَلَا عَلَى ٱلۡمَرِيضِ حَرَجٞۗ\nAllah mentions the legal reasons that allow one to be excused from joining Jihad, such as blindness, lameness, and various illnesses that last for days then end. When one is ill, he is allowed to remain behind and will have a valid excuse to do so, until his illness ends. Ibn Kathir: 4/193.\nGiven this verse, if Jihad is obligatory, then what are the legal excuses for missing it?\nوَمَن يَتَوَلَّ يُعَذِّبۡهُ عَذَابًا أَلِيمٗا ١٧\nIn this life with humiliation and in the Hereafter with the Fire. Ibn Kathir: 4/193.\nIs painful punishment limited to the Hereafter?\n۞لَّقَدۡ رَضِيَ ٱللَّهُ عَنِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ إِذۡ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحۡتَ ٱلشَّجَرَةِ فَعَلِمَ مَا فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡ فَأَنزَلَ ٱلسَّكِينَةَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَأَثَٰبَهُمۡ فَتۡحٗا قَرِيبٗا ١٨\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"None of those who gave the pledge under the tree shall enter the Fire.\" (And He knew what was in their hearts), their true faith and determination in fulfilling their pledge. (And rewarded them with an imminent conquest), the conquest of Khaibar. It is also said that it is the conquest of Makkah, however, the former interpretation is more prominent. Allah rewarded them with this conquest as well as the reward in the Hereafter. Ibn Juzay: 2/349.\nGiven this verse, how do you respond to those who believe that all the Companions are disbelievers except seven of them?\nوَعَدَكُمُ ٱللَّهُ مَغَانِمَ كَثِيرَةٗ تَأۡخُذُونَهَا\nAllah is subtle in His plan, where He can make you attain great things through the opposite of their causes as people would expect. Hence, the believer should never fear the great number of those who oppose him or their overwhelming power. Following the path of Allah in righteous deeds with steadfastness in faith is the real cause of victory, and this is a conditional relationship, which can attained through visible or non-visible means. Al-Biqai: 18/319.\nAllah decrees for the believer far better than his own choice. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَعَدَكُمُ ٱللَّهُ مَغَانِمَ كَثِيرَةٗ تَأۡخُذُونَهَا فَعَجَّلَ لَكُمۡ هَٰذِهِۦ\nAllah promises His believing servants abundant booties that He will give them until the Day of Resurrection, and they will take them at the specified times decreed by Him. Al-Shawkani: 5/51.\nExplain how Allah honors the believers among this Ummah.\nوَكَفَّ أَيۡدِيَ ٱلنَّاسِ عَنكُمۡ وَلِتَكُونَ ءَايَةٗ لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ\n(And He has restrained people's hands from you), when the Prophet (ﷺ) went and besieged Khaibar, Arab tribes from Asad and Ghatafan planned to raid the Muslim families and children in Madinah, but Allah restrained their hands by casting horror into their hearts. Al-Baghawi: 4/175.\nWhat is meant by restraining people's hands?\nسُنَّةَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلَّتِي قَدۡ خَلَتۡ مِن قَبۡلُۖ وَلَن تَجِدَ لِسُنَّةِ ٱللَّهِ تَبۡدِيلٗا ٢٣\nHaving described His way as established in the past, Allah affirms its continuity in the future to be the norm at all times by saying, (And never will you find in the way of Allah any change), because the constancy of that victory among all nations throughout history and relating it by Allah through His Messengers and Prophets indicate Allah’s support for His groups where no one can prevent the Will of Allah. Ibn Ashur: 26/183.\nWhat is the reason for this affirmation: (And never will you find in the way of Allah any change)?\nwords\nحَرَجٌA sin in abandoning Jihad\nيُبَايِعُونَكَAl-Ridwan allegiance at Al-Hudaybiya\nالسَّكِينَةَTranquility\nفَتحًا قَرِيبًاAn imminent conquest\nأَحَاطَ اللهُ بِهَاHe has full control over them\nلَوَلَّوُا الأَدبَارَThey would have turned their backs in defeat\nسُنَّةَ اللهِThe way of Allah"],[514,"§Al-Fath\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, send down tranquility upon my heart.\"\nHelp a Muslim brother with whom you have no kinship ties.\nAlways say, \"If Allah wills,\" when you speak about things in the future.\nguid\nAllah has prevented the punishment of the disbelievers in Makkah due to some believers living among them, for the believer's life is sacred to Allah.\nAllah's wisdom in delaying some good was manifested in the conquest of Makkah.\nThe Prophet's Companions (j) are honored by Allah, so revere them and oppose those who are hostile to them such as the Shiat and akin to them.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡلَا رِجَالٞ مُّؤۡمِنُونَ وَنِسَآءٞ مُّؤۡمِنَٰتٞ لَّمۡ تَعۡلَمُوهُمۡ أَن تَطَـُٔوهُمۡ فَتُصِيبَكُم مِّنۡهُم مَّعَرَّةُۢ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖۖ لِّيُدۡخِلَ ٱللَّهُ فِي رَحۡمَتِهِۦ مَن يَشَآءُۚ لَوۡ تَزَيَّلُواْ لَعَذَّبۡنَا ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِنۡهُمۡ عَذَابًا أَلِيمًا ٢٥\nA servant may think that his happiness would be in attaining a particular thing, but Allah makes it difficult for him to attain because He knows it will have evil consequences for His servant. Hence, Allah's prevention is, in fact, a mercy toward the servant despite appearing as a deprivation. So, hold fast to submission to Allah in all affairs while striving to do good deeds at all times. This verse, also, shows that Allah may ward off His punishment from the disbeliever to save the believer. Al-Biqai: 18/329.\nAllah's decree is tied to His wisdom and mercy. Explain in light of this verse.\nإِذۡ جَعَلَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فِي قُلُوبِهِمُ ٱلۡحَمِيَّةَ حَمِيَّةَ ٱلۡجَٰهِلِيَّةِ\nLinking pride to ignorance is to disdain and degrade it, for it is a characteristic of people from the times of ignorance. In Quran terminology, this linkage is meant as a censure; similar to saying, (Thinking of Allah other than the truth - the thought of ignorance) [3:154], and (Do they seek the judgment of the times of ignorance) [5:50]. Ibn Ashur: 26/194.\nWhat is the benefit of linking pride to ignorance?\nفَأَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ سَكِينَتَهُۥ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِۦ وَعَلَى ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ\nThis tranquility results in certain faith in the news from Allah, and full submission to Allah's orders, where no doubt would be cast on His news, and no will would counter His orders. Repelling the evil prompts that pass through the servant's heart, as a test for him, strengthens his faith and raises high his rank with Allah. The mere existence of these evil prompts never reflects that the servant has a low rank with Allah. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/459.\nWhat is the result of sending down Allah's tranquility upon the believers' hearts?\nإِذۡ جَعَلَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فِي قُلُوبِهِمُ ٱلۡحَمِيَّةَ حَمِيَّةَ ٱلۡجَٰهِلِيَّةِ فَأَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ سَكِينَتَهُۥ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِۦ وَعَلَى ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَأَلۡزَمَهُمۡ كَلِمَةَ ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰ\nThe pride of ignorance entails words and actions that were suited for its purpose, hence, Allah has put tranquility in the hearts of His allies to counter the pride of ignorance and put the word of piety on their tongues to counter the word of wickedness prompted by the pride of ignorance. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/458-459.\nAllah bestowed tranquility and word of piety upon the believers. Why?\nوَأَلۡزَمَهُمۡ كَلِمَةَ ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰ\nThe word of piety is: \"None is worthy of worship but Allah alone.\" It is linked to piety because it shields one from shirk, and it is the apex of every piety. Al-Alusi: 13/271.\nWhat is meant by (the word of piety)? Why does every believer adhere to it?\nلَّقَدۡ صَدَقَ ٱللَّهُ رَسُولَهُ ٱلرُّءۡيَا بِٱلۡحَقِّۖ لَتَدۡخُلُنَّ ٱلۡمَسۡجِدَ ٱلۡحَرَامَ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ\nThis alludes to the fact that the time when they enter the Sacred Mosque would be in accordance with His Will, and not due to their plans or strength. Al-Alusi: 13/273.\nIn this verse, Allah's will is mentioned to indicate something. What is it?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَرۡسَلَ رَسُولَهُۥ بِٱلۡهُدَىٰ وَدِينِ ٱلۡحَقِّ لِيُظۡهِرَهُۥ عَلَى ٱلدِّينِ كُلِّهِۦۚ\nIn many instances, the Quran mentions the power of knowledge and that of physical strength, as saying, (It is He Who has sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth, to make it prevail over all religions), where guidance is the comprehensive knowledge, and the religion of truth is the comprehensive action; it is similar to this verse, (men of strength and insight)[38:45]. Ibn Taimyah: 6/38.\nA Muslim needs two kinds of powers. What are they?\nwords\nبِبَطنِ مَكَّةَAt Al-Hudaybiya near Makkah\nأَظفَرَكُمHe caused you to overcome them\nمَعكُوفًاPrevented\nمَحِلَّهُIts place of sacrifice\nمَعَرَّةٌSin, dishonor\nتَزَيَّلُواThe believers and disbelievers were separate\nالحَمِيَّةَPride"],[515,"§Al-Fath, Al-Hujurat\ndeeds\nSmile at your collegues and brothren and greet them with salam, for it is part of mercy among yourselves.\nToday, take more time in bowing and prostrating.\nSay, \"O Allah, guide me to the best of sayings, deeds, and qualities, for only You guide me to their best. Protect me from the worst of them, for only You protect me from their worst.\"\nguid\nThe followers of the Messenger (ﷺ) are firm against the disbelievers, merciful among themselves.\nThe Prophet's (ﷺ) rank is very high, hence, a Muslim must exhibit politeness when mentioning his name and ask Allah to confer His blessing upon him.\nIntellect is linked to civility.\nrefl\nمُّحَمَّدٞ رَّسُولُ ٱللَّهِۚ وَٱلَّذِينَ مَعَهُۥٓ أَشِدَّآءُ عَلَى ٱلۡكُفَّارِ رُحَمَآءُ بَيۡنَهُمۡۖ تَرَىٰهُمۡ رُكَّعٗا سُجَّدٗا يَبۡتَغُونَ فَضۡلٗا مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرِضۡوَٰنٗاۖ\nIn combining these two opposite qualities -firmness and mercy-, Allah alludes to the originality of judgment and the wisdom in their reasoning. They maintain their attitudes and conduct their deeds maturely and wisely so that not a single quality dominates them at all times, nor will they rush to act inherently or without vision. Ibn Ashur: 26/205.\nWhat is the benefit of combining the believers' descriptions, firmness and mercy?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ مَعَهُۥٓ أَشِدَّآءُ عَلَى ٱلۡكُفَّارِ رُحَمَآءُ بَيۡنَهُمۡۖ تَرَىٰهُمۡ رُكَّعٗا سُجَّدٗا\n(Firm against the disbelievers), they are serious and strive hard in opposing them, putting their utmost effort into achieving that. (Merciful among themselves), loving one another, showing mercy and kindness to one another, like a single body; each of them loves for his brother what he loves for himself. This is how they treat one another. As for their interactions with their Creator, (You see them bowing and prostrating [in prayer]). Al-Saadi: 795.\nAfter mentioning the believers' firmness against the disbelievers and their mercy toward the believers, Allah mentions their prayers. Why ?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُقَدِّمُواْ بَيۡنَ يَدَيِ ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦۖ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٞ ١\nIf Allah, the Almighty, forbids them from raising their voices over the Messenger's (ﷺ) voice, so how would it be for raising their opinions over his teachings that he brought from Allah?! Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/5.\nThis verse indicates that sound reason should follow the true revelation. Explain.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُقَدِّمُواْ بَيۡنَ يَدَيِ ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦۖ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٞ ١\nThis is an emphatic prohibition on giving precedence to any view over that of the Messenger (ﷺ) for once the Sunnah of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) is clear, it becomes obligatory to follow and give precedence to it over everything else, no matter what it is. Al-Saadi: 799.\nWhat is the Sharia ruling on following other than the clear sayings of the Messenger (ﷺ)?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَرۡفَعُوٓاْ أَصۡوَٰتَكُمۡ فَوۡقَ صَوۡتِ ٱلنَّبِيِّ وَلَا تَجۡهَرُواْ لَهُۥ بِٱلۡقَوۡلِ كَجَهۡرِ بَعۡضِكُمۡ لِبَعۡضٍ\nSome scholars disliked raising voices when visiting the Prophet's (ﷺ) gravesite. Moreover, some scholars disliked raising voices while sitting with scholars in study circles; this is to honor them, as they are the inheritors of the Prophets. Al-Qurtubi: 19/361.\nWhat is the practical implementation of this verse?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَرۡفَعُوٓاْ أَصۡوَٰتَكُمۡ فَوۡقَ صَوۡتِ ٱلنَّبِيِّ وَلَا تَجۡهَرُواْ لَهُۥ بِٱلۡقَوۡلِ كَجَهۡرِ بَعۡضِكُمۡ لِبَعۡضٍ\nThe obvious meaning of this verse is that one's deeds may become worthless without him realizing it. Al-Shanqiti: 7/403.\nDo you understand from this verse that one's deeds may become worthless without him realizing it?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُنَادُونَكَ مِن وَرَآءِ ٱلۡحُجُرَٰتِ أَكۡثَرُهُمۡ لَا يَعۡقِلُونَ ٤\nAllah criticized them for their lack of understanding, because they did not understand His command to observe etiquette with His Messenger (ﷺ) and show him respect, for it is a sign of intellect to be polite and observe etiquette. A person's manners are a sign of intellect, and indicate that Allah intends good for him. Al-Saadi: 799.\nWhat is the link between intellect and politeness in light of this verse?\nwords\nسِيمَاهُمTheir mark\nشَطأَهُIts shoot, branch\nفَآزَرَهُMakes it strong\nفَاستَغلَظَGrows thick\nفَاستَوَى عَلَى سُوقِهِStands straight on its stem\nلاَ تُقَدِّمُواDo not decide any matter of importance before Allah and His Messenger"],[516,"§Al-Hujurat\ndeeds\nVisit a friend or help him in getting something done and supplicate Allah for him so that the meaning of brotherhood, ordained by Allah, is realized.\nMake peace between two feuding friends of yours.\nCall your friend or brother by the most likable name to him.\nguid\nEndearing faith and righteous deeds, and hating disbelief and defiance is a blessing from Allah that He gives to whomever He wills, so ask Him for it.\nBe fair and just in all of your affairs.\nPersist in repentance and submitting to Allah.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِن جَآءَكُمۡ فَاسِقُۢ بِنَبَإٖ فَتَبَيَّنُوٓاْ أَن تُصِيبُواْ قَوۡمَۢا بِجَهَٰلَةٖ فَتُصۡبِحُواْ عَلَىٰ مَا فَعَلۡتُمۡ نَٰدِمِينَ ٦\nA piece of information, provided by a defiantly disobedient person, is subject to suspicion and fabrication due to his weak adherence to the religion. This weakness induces him to disparage the forbidden and belittle whatever information he passes around or a testimony that may harm others or the general public. His audacity to do such things will continue to increase unless he repents, shows regrets, and desist from that. Ibn Ashur: 26/231.\nWhy are enjoined to verify the information provided by a defiantly disobedient person?\nوَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ فِيكُمۡ رَسُولَ ٱللَّهِۚ لَوۡ يُطِيعُكُمۡ فِي كَثِيرٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡأَمۡرِ لَعَنِتُّمۡ\n(If he were to obey you in much of the matter, you would be in difficulty), you would have suffered. If the word \"obeyed you\" were used instead of (were to obey you), it would indicate they wanted him always to obey them, which is not true. It is their duty to obey him, and not the opposite, because his views are better and truer than that of others. If he would follow people's views, they would perish. It is their duty follow and obey him, as indicated by this verse: (But Allah has endeared to you the faith). Ibn Juzay: 2/375.\nIt is inferred by this verse that making laws that are contrary to that of Islamic Sharia leads to difficulty and destruction. Explain.\nوَلَٰكِنَّ ٱللَّهَ حَبَّبَ إِلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡإِيمَٰنَ وَزَيَّنَهُۥ فِي قُلُوبِكُمۡ وَكَرَّهَ إِلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡكُفۡرَ وَٱلۡفُسُوقَ وَٱلۡعِصۡيَانَۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلرَّٰشِدُونَ ٧\nA rightly guided is being steadfast in truth. Attaining the right guidance is by pursuing the truth, as Allah takes upon Himself to guide and make successful those who strive against their own whims; He says, (And those who strive in Our cause, We will surely guide them to Our ways, for Allah is certainly with those who do good)[29:69]. Al-Biqai: 7/229.\nThe right guidance is a high stage of faith. How can the servant attain it?\nإِنَّمَا ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ إِخۡوَةٞ\nMeaning: They are brothers in religion, not in kinship. That is why it is said that brotherhood of religion is stronger than that of kinship, for the brotherhood of kinship can be severed between individuals of different religions while the brotherhood of religion cannot be severed between individuals with no kinship ties. Al-Qurtubi: 19/383.\nWhich is stronger: Brotherhood of religion or that of kinship? Why?\nإِنَّمَا ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ إِخۡوَةٞ فَأَصۡلِحُواْ بَيۡنَ أَخَوَيۡكُمۡۚ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُرۡحَمُونَ ١٠\nThe word (mercy) is chosen because the dealing among brothers is based on mercy, hence, its recompense is receiving mercy from Allah. Ibn Ashur: 26/245.\nWhy is the word (mercy) chosen in this verse?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا يَسۡخَرۡ قَوۡمٞ مِّن قَوۡمٍ عَسَىٰٓ أَن يَكُونُواْ خَيۡرٗا مِّنۡهُمۡ وَلَا نِسَآءٞ مِّن نِّسَآءٍ عَسَىٰٓ أَن يَكُنَّ خَيۡرٗا مِّنۡهُنَّۖ\nThe righteous predecessors avoided ridicule by all means. Amr bin Shurahbil said: If I saw a man suckling a goat and I laughed at him, I would fear doing what he did. Abdullah bin Masoud said: Affliction comes from loose talk; if I ridicule a dog, I would fear being turned into one. Al-Qurtubi: 19/383.\nHow did the righteous predecessors practice the Quran? Explain in light of the meaning of this verse.\nوَلَا تَلۡمِزُوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمۡ\nMeaning: Do not backbite one another and do not slander one another, but here Allah says (And do not insult yourselves), so He makes the insult to a brother like an insult to oneself because the believers are like one person in regard to their duties toward each other such as self-reforming and wishing the best for each other. This meaning is clarified in the words of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ), \"The believers are like one body; when one of the limbs aches, the whole body aches with fever and sleeplessness.\" Al-Tabari: 22/298.\nThe verse uses the term, (yourselves). Why? Does man insult himself?!\nwords\nبِنَبَإٍNews\nفَتَبَيَّنُواVerify the news\nلَعَنِتُّمYou would be in difficulty\nبَغَتTransgresses\nتَفِيءَThey submit to the rule of Allah\nوَلاَ تَلمِزُواDo not insult one another\nوَلاَ تَنَابَزُوا بِالأَلقَابِDo not call one another by offensive nicknames"],[517,"§Al-Hujurat\ndeeds\nRecall a person about whom you had a negative assumption and find him an excuse.\nRecall a person whom you had backbitten, seek Allah's forgiveness and supplicate Allah for him.\nStrive with your wealth in the cause of Allah by spending part of it for charity.\nguid\nThe diversity of people and tribes is meant for knowing each other, not for division, dispute, or racism.\nDifferentiating people based on anything but righteousness is a sign of ignorance and heedlessness.\nIf Allah gives you success in doing a righteous deed, thank Him and never consider it a favor to Him because He can deprive you of it.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱجۡتَنِبُواْ كَثِيرٗا مِّنَ ٱلظَّنِّ إِنَّ بَعۡضَ ٱلظَّنِّ إِثۡمٞۖ وَ لَا تَجَسَّسُواْ\nAt first, a person may have a suspicion about something, so he would start spying, searching, watching, and listening in order to investigate his suspicion. Hence, the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade that. It is fair to say that suspicions that have no valid telltale signs must be avoided. Al-Qurtubi: 19/396.\nWhat are the forbidden suspicions according to Sharia?\nوَلَا يَغۡتَب بَّعۡضُكُم بَعۡضًاۚ أَيُحِبُّ أَحَدُكُمۡ أَن يَأۡكُلَ لَحۡمَ أَخِيهِ مَيۡتٗا فَكَرِهۡتُمُوهُۚ\nAbu Qilaba Al-Raqashi said: I heard Aba A'sim saying: I have never backbite anyone since I knew what backbiting may entail. Maimun [bin Mahran] never used to backbite anyone, nor let someone do that in his presence, or else he would leave the place. Al-Qurtubi: 19/404.\nNarrate two examples of how the righteous predecessors warned against backbiting.\nوَلَا يَغۡتَب بَّعۡضُكُم بَعۡضًاۚ أَيُحِبُّ أَحَدُكُمۡ أَن يَأۡكُلَ لَحۡمَ أَخِيهِ مَيۡتٗا فَكَرِهۡتُمُوهُۚ\nAllah likens backbiting to eating dead flesh because the dead is not aware of being eaten just like the absent person is not aware of being defamed. Ibn Abbas (k) said: Allah presents this example for backbiting because eating dead flesh is prohibited and revolting, and so is backbiting which is prohibited in religion and abhorrent to the souls. Qatadah said: As any of you would never eat the flesh of his dead brother, he must refrain from backbiting him alive. Al-Qurtubi: 19/403.\nThe example of backbiting is like eating the flesh of the dead. How?\nوَلَا يَغۡتَب بَّعۡضُكُم بَعۡضًاۚ أَيُحِبُّ أَحَدُكُمۡ أَن يَأۡكُلَ لَحۡمَ أَخِيهِ مَيۡتٗا فَكَرِهۡتُمُوهُۚ\nOmar bin Al-Khattab (t) said: Beware of mentioning people, for it is like sickness; and focus on remembering Allah, for it is a healing. Ali bin Alhusain (k) heard someone backbiting another, so he said: Beware of backbiting because it is food for the dogs among people. Some people said to Amr bin Obaid: We heard someone was backbiting you so much that we felt merciful toward you. He replied: You should have been merciful toward him. A man said to Alhasan: I was told that you backbit me, he replied: To me, you are not worth putting you in control of good deeds. Al-Qurtubi: 19/404.\nState the saying of one of the righteous predecessors about backbiting.\nوَلَا يَغۡتَب بَّعۡضُكُم بَعۡضًاۚ أَيُحِبُّ أَحَدُكُمۡ أَن يَأۡكُلَ لَحۡمَ أَخِيهِ مَيۡتٗا\nThe basis for prohibiting backbiting is the brotherhood of faith, hence, its prohibition is strengthened commensurate with the believer's level of faith; the greater faith he has, the more incriminating is to backbite him. Ibn Taimyah: 6/62.\nIs backbiting the believers the same for all of them? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَجَعَلۡنَٰكُمۡ شُعُوبٗا وَقَبَآئِلَ لِتَعَارَفُوٓاْۚ إِنَّ أَكۡرَمَكُمۡ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ أَتۡقَىٰكُمۡۚ\nAllah makes clear that He made people into nations and tribes so that they may be able to know and differentiate one another, not to feel haughty toward each other and transgress against others. The fact that some are better than others is due to reasons other than lineage, and Allah makes clear this fact by saying, (Indeed, the most noble of you before Allah is the most righteous). Hence, nobility and distinguishment among people are based on righteousness, not on lineage. Al-Shanqiti: 7/417.\nThis verse clarifies and sets right the criteria of distinguishment among people. Explain.\nإِنَّمَا ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ ثُمَّ لَمۡ يَرۡتَابُواْ وَجَٰهَدُواْ بِأَمۡوَٰلِهِمۡ وَأَنفُسِهِمۡ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ\n(Indeed, the believers), the true believers are those who combine faith and Jihad in His cause, because if a person strives against the disbelievers, that is indicative of complete faith in his heart, for whoever strives against others in support of Islam and striving to establish its laws, it is more likely that he will strive against himself to establish Islam and its laws in his own life. Al-Saadi: 802.\nIn this verse, Allah combines faith and Jihad for the true believer. Why?\nwords\nكَثِيرًا مِنَ الظَّنِّNegative assumption about the believers\nوَلاَ تَجَسَّسُواDo not spy on one another\nوَلاَ يَغتَبDo not backbite one another\nوَقَبَائِلَTribes\nالأَعرَابُThe Bedouins\nلاَ يَلِتكُم مِن أَعمَالِكُمHe will not detract anything from the reward of your deeds"],[518,"§Qaf\ndeeds\nGive a verbal or written advice to a heedless Muslim.\nLook at the mountains or the seas and write two useful lessons inspired by your reflection about the manifestations of Allah's might and power.\nLook at a dead tree, then reflect on the stages through which it went, and compare that to the stages through which you will go through in your life.\nguid\nThe Quran is Glorious and so are those who adhere to its teachings.\nThe Oneness of Allah is inferred by His Lordship of all things.\nThe One Who is capable of the first creation is certainly capable of bringing it back after death.\nrefl\nسورة قٓۚ\nThis Surah contains many foundations of faith, which made the Prophet (ﷺ) recite it during great Muslim gatherings such as Friday and Eid prayers. He used to recite it often, especially in Fajr prayer. Ibn Taimyah: 6/83.\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) used to recite this Surah during great Muslim gatherings. Why?\nقٓۚ وَٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ ٱلۡمَجِيدِ ١\n(Glorious) indicates that it has numerous, great attributes. The best thing to be described in such terms is this Quran, and this makes it obligatory to follow it in the most perfect manner, to hasten to implement its teachings and to show gratitude to Allah for blessing us with it. Al-Saadi: 803.\nThe Quran is described as (Glorious), what does this description entail?\nبَلۡ كَذَّبُواْ بِٱلۡحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمۡ فَهُمۡ فِيٓ أَمۡرٖ مَّرِيجٍ ٥\nQatadah said about this verse: Whoever abandons the truth, his affairs will be in a state of confusion, and his faith will be obscured. Alhasan said: Whenever people neglect the truth, they will end up in a state of confusion. Al-Qurtubi: 21/316.\nWhat is the reason for some people to be in a state of confusion?\nأَفَلَمۡ يَنظُرُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱلسَّمَآءِ فَوۡقَهُمۡ كَيۡفَ بَنَيۡنَٰهَا وَزَيَّنَّٰهَا وَمَا لَهَا مِن فُرُوجٖ ٦\nMeaning: Looking at it does not require any effort or travel, rather, it is very easy. Let them see (how We have built it) like a smooth dome, well-built and adorned with stars, stretching from one horizon to the other in the most beautiful manner. No defect, gaps or flaws can be seen in it. Allah has made it a roof for the people of the earth, and He placed in it things that serve essential interests for them. Al-Saadi: 804.\nAllah describes the heavens as above the people despite their knowledge of it. Why?\nتَبۡصِرَةٗ وَذِكۡرَىٰ لِكُلِّ عَبۡدٖ مُّنِيبٖ ٨\nEven though everyone may benefit from the mention of the earth’s affairs, the servant who turns to Allah is singled out for the insight and reminder because he truly benefits from it and he is the focus for mentioning the wisdom of these actions. In this verse, there is an honor to the believers and an allusion to the disbelievers’ neglect of the insight and reminder. Ibn Ashur: 26/291.\nThe servant who turns to Allah is singled out for insight and reminder. Why?\nوَنَزَّلۡنَا مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءٗ مُّبَٰرَكٗا فَأَنۢبَتۡنَا بِهِۦ جَنَّٰتٖ وَحَبَّ ٱلۡحَصِيدِ ٩ وَٱلنَّخۡلَ بَاسِقَٰتٖ لَّهَا طَلۡعٞ نَّضِيدٞ ١٠ رِّزۡقٗا لِّلۡعِبَادِۖ وَأَحۡيَيۡنَا بِهِۦ بَلۡدَةٗ مَّيۡتٗاۚ كَذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡخُرُوجُ ١١\nThe verse indicates that it is befitting for the servant to benefit from the insight and reminder that this blessing provides more than his benefit from it as provision only. Al-Alusi: 13/327.\nWhat is the most important benefit for the believer from the rain?\nكَذَّبَتۡ قَبۡلَهُمۡ قَوۡمُ نُوحٖ وَأَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلرَّسِّ وَثَمُودُ ١٢ وَعَادٞ وَفِرۡعَوۡنُ وَإِخۡوَٰنُ لُوطٖ ١٣ وَأَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡأَيۡكَةِ وَقَوۡمُ تُبَّعٖۚ كُلّٞ كَذَّبَ ٱلرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ وَعِيدِ ١٤\nThis is a consolation to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). It is as if saying: Do not grieve, nor be distressed for their denial, as it was the same for all the Prophets before you; their people denied them, and none followed them except a few. Al-Shawkani: 5/73.\nWhat do preachers and those who enjoin what is good and forbid what is evil benefit from this verse?\nwords\nمَرِيجٍA state of confusion\nفُرُوجٍRifts, cracks\nزَوجٍ بَهِيجٍA pleasant kind\nوَحَبَّ الحَصِيدِGrain for harvest\nبَاسِقَاتٍLofty\nطَلعٌ نَضِيدٌClustered fruit\nالرَّسِّThe name of a well\nأَفَعَيِينَاWere We wearied?!"],[519,"§Qaf\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the evil of myself and the evil of the devil and his call to Shirk (polytheism).\"\nSay, \"Glorified is Allah and praised is He; Glorified is Allah the Great,\" so that you will find it in the record of your deeds.\nVisit the cemetery and seek refuge with Allah from heedlessness.\nguid\nRecording the deeds by the angel-keepers enhances self-monitoring of the servant.\nBeware of being heedless of Allah, the Almighty.\nWithholding of good is a way to the Fire.\nrefl\nوَنَحۡنُ أَقۡرَبُ إِلَيۡهِ مِنۡ حَبۡلِ ٱلۡوَرِيدِ ١٦\nAllah states that He is closer to him than his jugular vein, which is the closest thing to a person; the jugular veins are the veins on both sides of the neck. This is a reminder to man to remember that his Creator is watching him; He sees what is in his heart and mind and is close to him in all situations. So, he should feel shy, lest Allah see him where He forbade him to be, or He not see him where He commanded him to be. Al-Saadi: 805.\nWhat is the wisdom behind mentioning the jugular vein? What do we learn from that?\nوَلَقَدۡ خَلَقۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ وَنَعۡلَمُ مَا تُوَسۡوِسُ بِهِۦ نَفۡسُهُۥۖ وَنَحۡنُ أَقۡرَبُ إِلَيۡهِ مِنۡ حَبۡلِ ٱلۡوَرِيدِ ١٦\nMeaning: The One Who created man and knows what his soul whispers within him, and He is closer to him than his jugular vein at the same time when the angel-keepers record his deeds, does not need these records because He is well aware of them and nothing is hidden from Him. However, He commanded the angel-keepers to record the deeds to establish proof against the servant on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Shanqiti: 7/426.\nWhat is the use of recording the servant's deeds while Allah is well aware of them?\nوَجَآءَتۡ سَكۡرَةُ ٱلۡمَوۡتِ بِٱلۡحَقِّۖ ذَٰلِكَ مَا كُنتَ مِنۡهُ تَحِيدُ ١٩\nThe verb: (Brought) is in past tense to indicate the certainty and nearness of its occurrence. Ibn Juzay: 2/365.\nIn this verse, the verb: (Brought) is in the past tense for an eloquent reason. What is it?\nيَوۡمَ نَقُولُ لِجَهَنَّمَ هَلِ ٱمۡتَلَأۡتِ وَتَقُولُ هَلۡ مِن مَّزِيدٖ ٣٠\nAbu Huraira narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said, \"Paradise and the Fire argued, and the Fire said, \"I have been given the privilege of receiving the arrogant and the tyrants.' Paradise said, 'What is the matter with me? Why do only the weak and the humble among the people enter me?' On that, Allah said to Paradise. 'You are My Mercy which I bestow on whoever I wish of my servants.' Then Allah said to the Fire, 'You are My (means of) punishment by which I punish whoever I wish of my servants; and each of you will have its fill.' As for the Fire, it will not be filled till Allah puts His Foot over it whereupon it will say, 'Enough! Enough!' At that time, it will be filled, its different parts will come closer to each other; and Allah will not wrong any of His created beings. As regards Paradise, Allah will create a new creation to fill it with.\" Al-Alusi: 26/471.\nDescribe the most prominent traits of people of Paradise and those of the Fire.\nهَٰذَا مَا تُوعَدُونَ لِكُلِّ أَوَّابٍ حَفِيظٖ ٣٢\nReturner), Ad-Dhahhak and others said: It means that he often returns to Allah from his sins, where he sins and repents. Ibn Abbas and Ata' said: He is the one who glorifies Allah, in reference to this verse, (O mountains. Glorify (Allah) with him! And the birds too)[34:10]. Al-Hakam bin Utaibah said: He is the one who remembers Allah in seclusion. Al-Shaabi and Mujahid said: He is the one who recalls his sins in seclusion and asks Allah for forgiveness; this is also said by Ibn Masoud. Obaid bin Omair said: It is he who, whenever sits in a place, asks for Allah's forgiveness. Moreover, he said: The returner and keeper is he who whenever leaves a place, he says, \"Glorified is Allah and praised is He, O Allah, I ask Your forgiveness from my sins in this sitting.\" Al-Baghawi: 19/454.\nList three of the traits of those who return to Allah.\nمَّنۡ خَشِيَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنَ بِٱلۡغَيۡبِ وَجَآءَ بِقَلۡبٖ مُّنِيبٍ ٣٣\n(Who feared the Most Merciful in the unseen), using the Holy Name, (the Most Merciful) to indicate that this person fears Allah while knowing He is the Most Merciful. Moreover, this alludes to the polytheists who deny His Holy Name, the Most Merciful, as related in this verse, (And when it is said to them, \"Prostrate to the Most Merciful,\" they say, \"And what is the Most Merciful?)[25:60]. Ibn Ashur: 26/320.\nWhat is the benefit of using the holy name (the Most Merciful) in this verse?\nوَجَآءَ بِقَلۡبٖ مُّنِيبٍ ٣٣\nMeaning: Even when people cannot see Him. This is the true fear of Allah. As for fearing Him in the presence of others, when they are looking at him, it may be pretentious and a show off, which does not indicate his true fear of Allah. Rather, the beneficial fear of Allah is the fear of Him when one is alone and when others are present. Al-Saadi: 807.\nFearing in the unseen is singled out for mention. Why?\nwords\nحَبلِ الوَرِيدِThe jugular vein\nرَقِيبٌ عَتِيدٌAn angel-observer prepared to record\nتَحِيدُYou avoid\nقَرِينُهُHis angel-companion who will testify against him\nمُعتَدٍAn aggressor\nمُرِيبٍDoubter of Allah's promise and threat\nمَا أَطغَيتُهُI did not mislead him\nوَأُزلِفَتِIt will be brought near\nمُنِيبٍReturning in repentance and obedience"]])